**Do not merge.** This branch merges every PR of the safety wave on top of main, so CI runs on the whole stack and the merge plan can be checked: #275, #278, #279, #287, #280, #281, #282, #283, #284, #285, #286, #293, #295, #289, #290, #297, #291, #292, #294, #296, #302, #300, #299, #298, #301 and #288 (head 45a1a53b, still in progress).

Each PR comes in as one merge commit whose message lists its conflicts and how they were resolved. A few small fix commits handle cases where two PRs are each correct alone but wrong together. The main ones:
- shell Kg was counted twice in 3D buckling (#283 × #290);
- #290's inclined-support refusals are superseded by #287;
- test oracles and tolerances needed updating.

The full merge plan is in `docs/MERGE_PLAN_SAFETY_WAVE.md`. It covers the recommended order, every conflict and its resolution (so each PR author can apply the same one), the behaviour changes for release notes, and what is still open.

Local results on this branch:
- engine `cargo test --release`: 7895 passed, 0 failed, 22 ignored;
- web `npm run test:unit`: 13739 passed, 0 failed;
- typecheck: no new errors;
- e2e smoke: see the plan.

The branch also includes a fix for main's red e2e test `ded-roundtrip` (it expected the old file keys).
